{"schemaVersion":1,"key":"ecosystem/inference-engines","track":"everyone","lang":"en","dir":"ltr","title":"Inference Engines","objectives":{"lang":"en","items":["Say what an inference engine is, and how it relates to a provider","Name the three reasons to run a model yourself, and when not to","Explain batching with a simple picture, and why it makes big providers cheap"]},"prerequisites":[{"key":"ecosystem/inference-providers","number":36,"title":"Inference Providers","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"}],"previous":{"key":"ecosystem/inference-providers","number":36,"title":"Inference Providers","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"next":{"key":"ecosystem/ui-design","number":38,"title":"UI Design","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"toc":[{"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","text":"Why This Matters to You","depth":2},{"id":"why-you-would-run-it-yourself","text":"Why You Would Run it Yourself","depth":2},{"id":"the-engines-by-the-size-of-the-problem","text":"The Engines, by the Size of the Problem","depth":2},{"id":"the-one-idea-that-explains-the-numbers","text":"The One Idea That Explains the Numbers","depth":2},{"id":"something-to-put-in-front-of-it","text":"Something to Put in Front of it","depth":2},{"id":"words-you-now-know","text":"Words You Now Know","depth":2},{"id":"summary","text":"Summary","depth":2},{"id":"references","text":"References","depth":2},{"id":"️-tools","text":"🛠️ Tools","depth":3},{"id":"️-repositories","text":"🗃️ Repositories","depth":3}],"body":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"ecosystem/inference-providers","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Inference Providers"}]},{"type":"text","text":" was about renting a model from a company. This module is about the software those companies run, and about when your own company might run it instead."}],"lead":true},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"inference engine"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the program that actually runs a model on a computer: it loads the model and turns your text into the answer. An inference provider is a company that runs one of these engines for you and charges per token."}]},{"type":"image","number":"37.1","title":"The Inference Engine Stack","note":"The engine is the middle layer: above it sits the model itself (its weights), below it the software layer and the chip that do the arithmetic. A provider runs all of this for you.","src":"course-images/ecosystem/inference-engine-layers.webp","alt":"The Inference Engine Stack","width":1600,"height":893},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why This Matters to You"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Sooner or later someone in your company will ask: \"should we run the AI ourselves, on our own servers?\" This module gives you the three good reasons, and the main reason not to."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-you-would-run-it-yourself","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why You Would Run it Yourself"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"There are three reasons, and only these three are worth the trouble."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"1. The data must not leave the company."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Health records, legal documents, and anything under a rule that says the text must stay inside. This is the most common reason by far."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"2. The volume makes it cheaper."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Paying per token is a very good deal at first. But at very large volume, renting your own machines and running the model yourself becomes cheaper."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"3. You need something no provider offers"}]},{"type":"text","text":", such as your own fine-tuned model from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/training","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Training LLMs"}]},{"type":"text","text":", a model nobody hosts, or full control over exactly which version runs, so an update never surprises you."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"If none of these is true, use a provider. Running models yourself is a real, ongoing job for a team, and in the first month you mostly learn what you forgot to budget for."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-engines-by-the-size-of-the-problem","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The Engines, by the Size of the Problem"}]},{"type":"diagram","number":"37.2","title":"The Engines, by the Size of the Problem","svg":{"light":"api/v1/diagrams/dcae5d7559a1cd6cf0aade0d8cff94fe.svg","dark":"api/v1/diagrams/e43e91825d0cd607585e02c794b09d95.svg"}},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"On one computer"}]},{"type":"text","text":", use the simple apps from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/llms","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LLM Fundamentals"}]},{"type":"text","text":": LM Studio or Ollama."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"On a company server with many users"}]},{"type":"text","text":", a proper serving engine: "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/vllm.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"vLLM"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the usual default. SGLang and NVIDIA's TensorRT-LLM are other names you will hear."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Across many machines"}]},{"type":"text","text":", a system such as "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/llm-d.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"llm-d"}]},{"type":"text","text":" coordinates them."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The map below shows where all of these sit, and where providers sit next to them."}]},{"type":"image","number":"37.3","title":"The LLM Inference Landscape","note":"Wing's map of the systems that serve AI models, read from the bottom: rented chips, the tools that manage them, the engines, then ways to share work between many machines. The inference-as-a-service column on the right is the provider route: those companies run the whole stack for you.","src":"course-images/ecosystem/llm-inference-landscape.webp","alt":"The LLM Inference Landscape","width":1213,"height":728},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-one-idea-that-explains-the-numbers","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The One Idea That Explains the Numbers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A computer that answers one request at a time is mostly waiting. So engines serve many requests together, which is called "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"batching"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Think of a bus instead of a taxi for each person: the trip costs about the same, but it carries many more people."}]},{"type":"image","number":"37.4","title":"Inference Server and Engine","note":"Requests arrive from an app and wait in a queue (the bus stop). The batching step fills the bus, and the model answers everyone together. The engine is only the inner box; the server around it manages the waiting line and keeps count of how things are going.","src":"course-images/ecosystem/inference-server-engine.webp","alt":"Inference Server and Engine","width":1400,"height":787},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The best engines do not even wait for the bus to fill: new requests join as soon as older ones finish, so the computer is never idle. This is one reason big providers can sell tokens cheaply: they fill every trip."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"something-to-put-in-front-of-it","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Something to Put in Front of it"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An engine gives programs a way to talk to it, but nothing for a person to look at. "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/open-webui-mono.svg","alt":"","mono":true},{"type":"text","text":"Open WebUI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the chat screen companies often put in front of their own model, so employees get something that looks and works like ChatGPT, running on the company's own computers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"words-you-now-know","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Words You Now Know"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Inference engine"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the program that actually runs a model."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Self-hosting"}]},{"type":"text","text":": running a model on your company's own computers."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"vLLM"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the usual engine for a company server."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Batching"}]},{"type":"text","text":": serving many requests together, like a bus instead of taxis."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Open WebUI"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a ChatGPT-like screen for a company's own model."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summary","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An inference engine runs the model; a provider is a company running one for you. Run it yourself only for one of three reasons: the data must stay inside, the volume is very large, or you need something no provider offers. Otherwise, rent. Batching is one reason large providers are cheap."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Quick check"}]},{"type":"text","text":": What is the most common reason a company runs a model itself? And why does batching make each token cheaper?"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"references","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"️-tools","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🛠️ Tools"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://ollama.com/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Ollama"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://lmstudio.ai/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LM Studio"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the simple apps for running a model on one computer"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"️-repositories","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🗃️ Repositories"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Open WebUI"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a chat screen to put in front of a company's own model"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"llm-d"}]},{"type":"text","text":": serving across many machines"}]}]}]}],"draft":null,"quiz":null}